 "answer": "**Yes—given your asthma, I’d stay indoors in Kuala Lumpur today, Saturday, October 17.** Available readings put the air in the unhealthy range, though they vary by station and index. Malaysia’s Health Ministry advises people with asthma to avoid going out when the official Air Pollutant Index (API) is above 100. ([aqicn.org](https://aqicn.org/city/kuala-lumpur/hk/%E2%80%9Chttps%3A/aqicn.org%E2%80%9C?utm_source=openai))\n\nKeep windows closed, avoid strenuous activity, and keep your usual asthma medicines and reliever inhaler close. Check Malaysia’s official APIMS readings for your area before deciding to go out; if you must, keep the trip brief. If you develop significant breathing difficulty or your reliever isn’t helping, seek urgent medical care. ([eqms.doe.gov.my](https://eqms.doe.gov.my/apims/main?utm_source=openai))",
